    "id": "train-3293",
    "question": "Carl is taking a class where the whole grade is based on four tests that are graded out of 100. He got an 80, a 75 and a 90 on his first three tests. If he wants an 85 average for the class, what is the minimum grade he needs to get on his last test?",
    "gold": "95",
    "answer": "First, find the total number of points Carl needs to earn across all the tests by multiplying his desired average by the number of tests: 85 * 4 = <<85*4=340>>340 marks.\nThen subtract all Carl's previous test scores to find the last score he needs to earn: 340 - 80 - 75 - 90 = <<340-80-75-90=95>>95 marks.\n#### 95"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the minimum grade Carl needs on his last test to achieve an average of 85, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total score Carl needs for all four tests to achieve an average of 85.\n2. Determine the sum of the scores Carl has already received on his first three tests.\n3. Find out how much more Carl needs on his last test to reach the total score required for the average.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total score Carl needs for all four tests to achieve an average of 85. The formula for the average is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average} = \\frac{\\text{Total Score}}{\\text{Number of Tests}}\n\\]\n\nGiven that the average is 85 and there are 4 tests, the total score required is:\n\n\\[\n85 \\times 4 = 340\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the sum of the scores Carl has already received on his first three tests. Carl's scores on the first three tests are 80, 75, and 90. So, the sum of these scores is:\n\n\\[\n80 + 75 + 90 = 245\n\\]\n\nTo find out the minimum grade Carl needs on his last test, we subtract the sum of his first three test scores from the total score required:\n\n\\[\n340 - 245 = 95\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the minimum grade Carl needs to get on his last test to achieve an average of 85 is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{95}\n\\]",
